cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "ISA Trace Lab"
abstract: >-
  ISA Trace Lab compiles a small language with Python syntax and 32-bit
  integers through an intermediate representation into machine code for
  documented subsets of RISC-V RV32I, MIPS32 Release 2, AArch64 (A64), and
  x86-64, executes the encoded bytes on instruction-set simulators, and records
  source-to-instruction mappings and execution traces. It runs as a static web
  application and as a headless TypeScript library and command-line tool.
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aalbata/isa-trace-lab"
authors:
  - family-names: "Al Bataineh"
    given-names: "Ali"
    affiliation: "Computer Information Science, Higher Colleges of Technology, Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9530-7950"
keywords:
  - instruction set architecture
  - RISC-V
  - MIPS
  - AArch64
  - x86-64
  - compiler
  - machine code
  - simulation
  - execution trace
